		}
		{
			title: "The Mech Boss"
			x: 5.25d
			y: -1.5d
			shape: "hexagon"
			description: [
				"&dMechBot was originally head of the FOP security training division, for their physical locations."
				""
				"&5He was apparently a big gym buff, and liked scrapping in various fight clubs he could find around the city. Wouldn't listen to you unless you could challenge him and beat him in an acceptable way."
				""
				"&dWhen the FOP moved everything digitally, he was brought along and given his own world: Iromine. He quickly took the form of MechBot, a super strong mecha that excels in both melee and ranged combat."
				""
				"&5He quickly implemented new protocols in the Iromine world. Strength is standing, the stronger you are the more say you have. And he offered challenges to anyone who could earn the Gold Spring battle pass."
			]
			dependencies: ["295B57EA4DC55761"]
			id: "3DA5A452C4D1186E"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7F52A8652373C121"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Challenging the Boss"
			x: 6.75d
			y: -2.25d
			shape: "diamond"
			subtitle: "BOSS FIGHT"
			description: [
				"&dIf you are wanting to face the MechBot head on, you'll need to find one of the MechBot Charging Pads, a sort of parking area for robots and MechBot to chill and recharge at. They look like helicopter landing pads in a way, four large platforms with a MechBot Altar on each pad."
				""
				"&5Right Click that Gold Spring on any MechBot Altar, and it will call MechBot over for a 1v1 (well, 1v however many you bring!) fight. "
				""
				"&dMechBot will start by chasing you down and fighting in melee if they can. Occasionally, they'll start jumping and dropping explosives as a counterattack. "
				""
				"&5As well, be careful as MechBot IS a mech, and thus fires the occasional missile at you."
				""
				"&dIf you manage to beat MechBot, as a winning prize you might get a gun or a strong hammer."
			]
			dependencies: ["3DA5A452C4D1186E"]
			id: "2761C1A297ED84A1"
			tasks: [{
				id: "1FA130318FD2E18B"
				type: "item"
				item: "kubejs:boss_card_mechbot"
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "036C5E18B3D2D7B0"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2245246540467579945L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Fighting Prowess"
			x: 6.75d
			y: -0.75d
			shape: "diamond"
			subtitle: "BOSS BRIBE"
			description: [
				"&5If you aren't inclined to fight a big mech, you can appease MechBot's fighting spirit by showing off your fighting ability."
				""
				"&dMy brother means you can give him various powerful 'trophies' to prove how strong you are. "
				""
				"&5He's one of those grizzled fighter types that loves to hear about good fights, cause it gives him ideas on who to challenge next."
				""
				"&dAnd if you GIVE him multiple of each trophy, it means that you liked the challenge enough that you have trophies to spare."
				""
				"&5Let's just not mention there are...less combative ways of getting some of these, yeah?"
				""
				"&dWell, the Dragon Scales you still have to hit the Ender Dragon WITH explosions, but not kill her so... I guess?"
			]
