		{
			title: "Powerful Construct"
			x: 3.0d
			y: 3.75d
			shape: "pentagon"
			description: [
				"&dThe Boss of Crystevia is Crystocore, a powerhungry FOP Boss that used to control multiple teams, each one dealing with a different field."
				""
				"&5They controlled these teams strictly, and pushed them to become the best by any means, which made Crystocore more powerful by connection."
				""
				"&dWhen the FOP Digitized, Crystocore was given control of Crystevia, which needed a powerful boss to control."
				""
				"&5Before anything, you'll need to create a Giant Crystal, a powerful gem, to get Crystocore's attention."
				""
				"&dExplore for a floating platform with a Crystal Extension Shrine in the center of it. You'll also need 10 of any Crystal, as well as a Rainbow Druse."
				""
				"&5Toss those Crystals down, then Right Click the Rainbow Druse onto the Crystal Extension Shrine. Bam, Giant Crystal!"
			]
			dependencies: ["6FAAA17351B67A7F"]
			id: "35F2AB6E06924EBC"
			tasks: [{
				id: "619D4F0EEB59763D"
				type: "item"
				item: "aoa3:giant_crystal"
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "46DA57D7DF2956C7"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 5632731352558517809L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "The Crystal Boss"
			x: 5.25d
			y: 3.75d
			shape: "hexagon"
			description: [
				"&dCrystocore, above all else, wants more power. And given they are now a giant crystal construct, on top of the power of status and control, they need other types of power too to keep growing stronger."
				""
				"&5It's why a lot of the Crystevia denizens are hostile, out of fear of Crystocore breaking them down and absorbing them. If they keep bringing sacrifices, well... they survive longer."
				""
				"&dWe aren't sure they realize they are stuck in the FOP Game Server. Many of the worlds they digitize and decimate never realize this, unfortunately..."
				""
				"&5That's why Crystocore has been given the nickname Construct of Power. All power, unending, relentless."
			]
			dependencies: ["35F2AB6E06924EBC"]
			id: "54727C73BD9B0004"
			tasks: [{
				id: "721100D290CD7CFD"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Power Struggle"
			x: 6.75d
			y: 3.0d
			shape: "diamond"
			subtitle: "BOSS BATTLE"
			description: [
				"&5If you are looking to destroy Crystocore, you're gonna want to find one of the Crystevia Power Stations."
				""
				"&dLook for a floating platform with a green block on top. This is the Power Station, which supplies power to some of the Crystevia citizens, but especially Crystocore themselves."
				""
				"&5That Giant Crystal you made? Right Click that onto the Power Station, and the energy from it will call forth Crystocore."
				""
				"&dCrystocore will fly around and charge at you. As well, every so often they'll change colors."
				""
				"&5Keep note of what color they are, Bandit. When they hit you, the color determines what effect you'll be hit with. Like Green is poison."
				""
				"&dSeriously, avoid Red. Ugh. But if you do defeat Crystocore, you might get a special crystal weapon."
			]
			dependencies: ["54727C73BD9B0004"]
			id: "39EA103830B9D647"
			tasks: [{
				id: "5B94884A9C4AF59D"
				type: "item"
				item: "kubejs:boss_card_crystocore"
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "35DDF7201F1ECDAD"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2245246540467579945L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Power Corrupts"
			x: 6.75d
			y: 4.5d
			shape: "diamond"
			description: [
				"&dIt doesn't sit right to just bribe and move on. Like Gyro, they are pretty bad, just look at how rough Crystevians are."
				""
				"&5How about...a Trojan Horse?"
				""
				"&d.Good idea, brother! Okay Bandit, Crystocore wants more power, let's provide power. A variety of energy generators is a good start."
				""
				"&5But what do we hide in the Horse?"
				""
				"&dHmm....Wait, make one generator a Gourmand generator. Consumes food for energy. And then grab some Poisonous Potatoes. It won't really hurt them, but it'll open up a way for a bunch of Nuke Virus' to hit Crystocore! You can find them in dungeon chests, drone delivery, or our Shop."
			]
			dependencies: ["54727C73BD9B0004"]
			id: "5EF503A6101951CC"
